8. What is an agent?
An agent is the machine or execution environment that runs the pipeline steps.
It can check out source code, run commands, compile, test, and publish artifacts.
Azure Pipelines
      ↓
     Agent
      ├── Check out code
      ├── Run commands
      ├── Build
      ├── Test
      └── Publish artifact

9. Organization and project
- Organization: The top-level Azure DevOps container.
- Project: A workspace within an organization.
Organization
   ├── Project A
   ├── Project B
   └── Project C
A project can contain Boards, Repos, Pipelines, Artifacts, and Test Plans. For this learning path, use one project to practise the workflow.

